#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explains what usage is and how to estimate how long a job that uses a primitive will take to run"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag kung ano ang usage at kung paano tantiyahin kung gaano katagal tatakbo ang isang job na gumagamit ng primitive"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workload usage"
msgstr "Paggamit ng workload"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "<span id=\"usage\"></span>\n"
#| "Usage represents consumption of the Qiskit Runtime service and is determined by the amount of time a QPU is locked to execute workloads.\n"
msgid ""
"<span id=\"usage\"></span>\n"
"Usage represents consumption of IBM Quantum Compute Service and is determined by the amount of time a QPU is locked to execute workloads.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"usage\"></span>\n"
"Ang usage ay kumakatawan sa pagkonsumo ng serbisyong Qiskit Runtime at tinutukoy ng dami ng oras na naka-lock ang QPU para sa pagpapatupad ng mga workload.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session usage is measured as the elapsed time while the session remains active, because QPU capacity is reserved for the duration of the session, regardless of whether workloads are actively running. See [Session length](/guides/run-jobs-session#session-length) for more information about session status transitions.\n"
msgstr "Ang session usage ay sinusukat bilang elapsed time habang nananatiling aktibo ang session, dahil ang kapasidad ng QPU ay nakalaan para sa buong tagal ng session, anuman ang kung aktibong tumatakbo ang mga workload. Tingnan ang [Session length](/guides/run-jobs-session#session-length) para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa mga transition ng status ng session.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batch usage is measured as the cumulative time the QPU is locked to execute all jobs in the batch.\n"
msgstr "Ang batch usage ay sinusukat bilang kabuuang oras na naka-lock ang QPU para ipagawa ang lahat ng job sa batch.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single job usage is measured as the time the QPU is locked to execute the job.\n"
msgstr "Ang single job usage ay sinusukat bilang oras na naka-lock ang QPU para ipagawa ang job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that failed or canceled jobs count toward your usage in certain circumstances - see the [Failed and canceled jobs](#failed-job) section for details.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang mga nabigo o nakanselong job ay maaaring mabilang sa iyong usage sa ilang partikular na sitwasyon — tingnan ang seksyong [Failed and canceled jobs](#failed-job) para sa mga detalye.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Pay-As-You-Go Plan users, see [Manage cost](/guides/manage-cost) for details on setting a cost limit.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga gumagamit ng Pay-As-You-Go Plan, tingnan ang [Manage cost](/guides/manage-cost) para sa mga detalye tungkol sa pagtatakda ng limitasyon sa gastos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"failed-job\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"failed-job\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage for failed and canceled jobs {#usage-for-failed-and-canceled-jobs}"
msgstr "Usage para sa mga nabigo at nakanselong job {#usage-for-failed-and-canceled-jobs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a job is failed or canceled, the reported usage is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Kapag nabigo o nakansela ang isang job, ang iniuulat na usage ay ang sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job or batch mode: If the failure or cancellation occurred because of a system error, the reported usage is zero. For jobs that failed due to user error or when a user canceled a job, the reported usage is any consumption that has occurred up to that point, including the overhead incurred to prepare the QPU to run the job.\n"
msgstr "Job o batch mode: Kung ang pagkabigo o pagkakansela ay nangyari dahil sa isang system error, ang iniuulat na usage ay zero. Para sa mga job na nabigo dahil sa user error o kapag nag-cancel ang isang user ng job, ang iniuulat na usage ay anumang konsumo na naganap hanggang sa puntong iyon, kasama na ang overhead na natamo para ihanda ang QPU na patakbuhin ang job.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session mode: The reported usage is the wall-clock time the session is active, regardless of the number of jobs that fail or are canceled.\n"
msgstr "Session mode: Ang iniuulat na usage ay ang wall-clock time habang aktibo ang session, anuman ang bilang ng mga job na nabigo o nakansela.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"view-usage\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"view-usage\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query a workload's actual usage {#query-a-workloads-actual-usage}"
msgstr "I-query ang aktwal na usage ng isang workload {#query-a-workloads-actual-usage}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After a workload has completed, there are several ways to view its actual usage:\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos makumpleto ang isang workload, may ilang paraan upang makita ang aktwal nitong usage:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "In `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.30 or later, run [`job.usage()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-job-v2#usage) for a single job, or [`batch.usage()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/batch#usage) or [`session.usage()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/session#usage) when using batch or session mode.  If using an older version of `qiskit-ibm-runtime` (>= 0.23 and < 0.30), the usage can be still be found in `session.details()[\"usage_time\"]` and `batch.details()[\"usage_time\"]`.\n"
msgstr "Sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.30 o mas bago, patakbuhin ang [`job.usage()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-job-v2#usage) para sa isang solong job, o ang [`batch.usage()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/batch#usage) o [`session.usage()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/session#usage) kapag gumagamit ng batch o session mode. Kung gumagamit ng mas lumang bersyon ng `qiskit-ibm-runtime` (>= 0.23 at < 0.30), mahahanap pa rin ang usage sa `session.details()[\"usage_time\"]` at `batch.details()[\"usage_time\"]`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use [`GET /sessions/{id}`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/sessions#tags__sessions__operations__get_session) to see usage for a specific batch or session (the endpoint is the same for both execution modes).\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang [`GET /sessions/{id}`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/sessions#tags__sessions__operations__get_session) para makita ang usage para sa isang partikular na batch o session (magkatulad ang endpoint para sa parehong execution mode).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use [`GET /jobs/{id}`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/jobs#tags__jobs__operations__get_job_metrics_jid) to see usage for a single job.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang [`GET /jobs/{id}`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/jobs#tags__jobs__operations__get_job_metrics_jid) para makita ang usage para sa isang solong job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"instance-usage\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"instance-usage\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "View instance usage {#view-instance-usage}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang usage ng instance {#view-instance-usage}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can view an instance's usage on the [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page, or, for those with the proper authority, the [Analytics](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/analytics) page.  Note that the pages might show different usage numbers because they calculate usage differently.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong tingnan ang usage ng isang instance sa pahina ng [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances), o, para sa mga may tamang awtoridad, sa pahina ng [Analytics](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/analytics). Tandaan na maaaring magpakita ang mga pahinang ito ng iba't ibang bilang ng usage dahil naiiba ang paraan ng pagkalkula ng bawat isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Instances page shows real-time usage for the last 28 days (rolling), up to the current time on the current day.  The Analytics page usage is re-calculated hourly and includes the last 28 full days; that is, it shows usage from 00:00 28 days ago to today, at the top of the hour.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng pahina ng Instances ang real-time na usage para sa nakaraang 28 araw (rolling), hanggang sa kasalukuyang oras sa kasalukuyang araw. Ang usage sa pahina ng Analytics ay muling kinakalkula bawat oras at kinabibilangan ng huling 28 buong araw; iyon ay, ipinapakita nito ang usage mula 00:00 ng 28 araw na nakalipas hanggang ngayon, sa simula ng oras.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimate usage before submitting a job {#estimate-usage-before-submitting-a-job}"
msgstr "Tantiyahin ang usage bago mag-submit ng job {#estimate-usage-before-submitting-a-job}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While getting an accurate local estimation is complicated by the extra operations done for error suppression and mitigation, you can use this baseline formula to get an approximation of estimated usage:\n"
msgstr "Habang ang pagkuha ng tumpak na lokal na pagtatantya ay kumplikado dahil sa mga karagdagang operasyong ginagawa para sa error suppression at mitigation, maaari mong gamitin ang baseline na formula na ito para makakuha ng tinatayang usage:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<per sub-job overhead> + (rep_delay + <circuit length>) * <num executions>`\n"
msgstr "`<per sub-job overhead> + (rep_delay + <circuit length>) * <num executions>`\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<per sub-job overhead>` is an overhead of approximately 2s per sub-job. This includes operations such as loading the payload into control electronics. Your primitive job may be divided into multiple sub-jobs if it is too large for the execution engine to process all at once.\n"
msgstr "Ang `<per sub-job overhead>` ay isang overhead na halos 2s bawat sub-job. Kasama dito ang mga operasyon tulad ng pag-load ng payload sa control electronics. Maaaring hatiin ang iyong primitive job sa maraming sub-job kung ito ay masyadong malaki para iproseso nang lahat sa isang pagkakataon ng execution engine.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rep_delay` is a [user-customizable](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-execution-options-v2#rep_delay) option, and the default is given by `backend.default_rep_delay`, which is 250 microseconds on most IBM Quantum backends. Note that lowering `rep_delay` decreases the total QPU execution time, but at the expense of increased state preparation error rate; see the [Dynamic repetition rate execution](/guides/repetition-rate-execution) guide for more information.\n"
msgstr "Ang `rep_delay` ay isang opsyong [maaaring i-customize ng gumagamit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-execution-options-v2#rep_delay), at ang default ay ibinibigay ng `backend.default_rep_delay`, na 250 microseconds sa karamihan ng IBM Quantum backend. Tandaan na ang pagbaba ng `rep_delay` ay nagpapababa ng kabuuang oras ng pagpapatupad ng QPU, ngunit sa gastos ng mas mataas na error rate sa state preparation; tingnan ang gabay na [Dynamic repetition rate execution](/guides/repetition-rate-execution) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- `<circuit length>` is the total instruction length. Each instruction takes different amount of time on the QPU, so the total length varies from circuit to circuit. A measurement, for example, can take 56 times longer than an `x` gate. `backend.target[<instruction>][<qubit>].duration` can be used to find the exact duration for each instruction. A typical circuit length is likely between 50-100 microseconds. If you are using error suppression or mitigation techniques with the primitives, extra instructions might be inserted into your circuit, which would increase the total circuit length.\n"
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    The [experimental `scheduler_timing` option](/guides/visualize-circuit-timing) returns the total circuit time, but this is NOT the time used for billing.\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
"- `<num executions>` is the total number of circuits times the number of shots, where the circuits are those generated after PUB elements are broadcasted.\n"
"    - If you are using error mitigation techniques with the primitives, extra circuits might be run as part of the mitigation process, which would increase the total number of executions. Additionally, advanced error mitigation techniques such as PEA and PEC come with much higher overhead because they require running circuits for noise learning.\n"
"    - Estimator groups qubit-wise commuting observables, which reduces the number of executions.\n"
msgstr ""
"- Ang `<circuit length>` ay ang kabuuang haba ng instruction. Bawat instruction ay gumagamit ng iba't ibang tagal ng oras sa QPU, kaya nagbabago ang kabuuang haba mula sa isang circuit patungo sa isa pa. Ang isang measurement, halimbawa, ay maaaring 56 beses na mas matagal kaysa sa isang `x` gate. Ang `backend.target[<instruction>][<qubit>].duration` ay maaaring gamitin para mahanap ang eksaktong tagal ng bawat instruction. Ang karaniwang haba ng circuit ay malamang nasa pagitan ng 50-100 microseconds. Kung gumagamit ka ng mga teknik na error suppression o mitigation sa mga primitive, maaaring may mga karagdagang instruction na idinagdag sa iyong circuit, na magpapataas ng kabuuang haba ng circuit.\n"
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    Ang [experimental na opsyong `scheduler_timing`](/guides/visualize-circuit-timing) ay nagbabalik ng kabuuang oras ng circuit, ngunit ito ay HINDI ang oras na ginagamit para sa billing.\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
"- Ang `<num executions>` ay ang kabuuang bilang ng mga circuit na pinarami sa bilang ng mga shot, kung saan ang mga circuit ay ang mga nabuong matapos i-broadcast ang mga PUB element.\n"
"    - Kung gumagamit ka ng mga teknik na error mitigation sa mga primitive, maaaring may mga karagdagang circuit na tatakbo bilang bahagi ng proseso ng mitigation, na magpapataas ng kabuuang bilang ng mga execution. Bukod pa rito, ang mga advanced na teknik na error mitigation tulad ng PEA at PEC ay may mas mataas na overhead dahil kailangan nilang magpatakbo ng mga circuit para sa noise learning.\n"
"    - Ang Estimator ay naggrugrupo ng mga qubit-wise commuting observable, na nagbabawas ng bilang ng mga execution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you aren't using any advanced error mitigation techniques or custom `rep_delay`, you can use `2+0.00035*<num executions>` as a quick formula.\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi ka gumagamit ng anumang advanced na teknik na error mitigation o custom na `rep_delay`, maaari mong gamitin ang `2+0.00035*<num executions>` bilang mabilis na formula.\n"

